ned (licenses). Runbook: Spark farm. Occupancy stays per node: Occupancy."],[356,"The **Your Spark** panel at the top of every docs page stores `SPARK_HOST` and friends in this browser. Highlighted chips in copyable commands are the same fields — click to edit. Copy buttons use those values. `--limit` defaults follow `DOWNLOAD_LIMIT` unless you override it on the widget."],[1551,"The `run` subcommand prints a **films/go-see / motion/silent/still-to-shot / motion/av/still-to-shot** Queue reminder for `--film go-see` (or still-here / switchyard). It does **not** POST graphs. It refuses MiniMax H3 names (`*h3*` / `*MiniMax*`)."],[923,"The Comfy venv"],[3474,"The constraint is SSH, not the demo"],[84,"The DCC ↔ Comfy **print** handshake (`guides/<slug>/<shot>/`)"],[2573,"The flex is a sugar pill"],[2163,"The generator App is occupancy **llm** (nothing GPU unless `llm-desk` is the writing desk). The **result** keeps the source occupancy (`klein` / `wan` / `ltx` / …). Open `_user/<slug>` and Queue only when that family is legal."],[1548,"The one-click **films/go-see** graph is sequential on one host. For a farm, load **motion/av/still-to-shot** (or optional **motion/silent/still-to-shot**) on each UI and **Queue** independent **5 s** shots — different beats in parallel. Concat locally:"],[1441,"The one-click film graph still prints **18 independent 5.00s latents**. Continuity is **last frame of shot N → start image of shot N+1**. One Queue runs them in order because each printer depends on the previous last frame."],[3528,"The one-sentence version"],[3295,"The original seven DCC graphs stay on `LoadImage` + `--install-inputs`. After a dump you can keep using those, or stay on `:8188` with the loaders."],[3604,"The PNG owns look. Prompt **motion + one camera verb** (`dolly in`, `pan`, `tracking`, `fixed camera`). Silent — do not prompt a score, foley, or dialogue."],[2254,"The rack emits at most one BPM token. Match `TextEncodeAceStepAudio1.5` BPM to that note. Do not also